{"name":"Raven’s Wing","hex":"#4b4045","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several, generally large, species of birds in the genus Corvus with lustrous black plumage; especially the common raven (Corvus corax).","A jet-black, often glossy, colour, like that of the plumage of a raven (etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the jet-black and often glossy colour of the plumage of a raven (etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raven"},{"term":"wing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An appendage of an animal's (bird, bat, insect) body that enables it to fly.","A fin at the side of a ray or similar fish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To injure slightly (as with a gunshot), especially in the wing or arm.","To fly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raven's Wing","blocks":[{"text":"Raven's Wing is a collection of 18 short stories by Joyce Carol Oates, published by E. P. Dutton in 1986."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/66/Raven%27s_Wing%2C_Joyce_Carol_Oates%2C_E._P._Dutton_publisher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raven's_Wing","wikidata":"Q123515621"},{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"http